// A test source without phase drift : the sine of an integer phase.
// os.osc accumulates a real phase, whose rounding drifts in single precision : after one
// second the float and double renders are out of phase, and only their levels compare.
// Here the phase is an integer counter m = (m + p) mod N, with an integer step p and
// N = 10 * SR : m < 2^24, exact in float and in double, and the step p = round(10 f)
// depends on the constant f only, never on SR, so both renders read the same phase at
// every sample and play exactly f Hz (f with at most one decimal). They differ only by
// the rounding of 2 pi m / N and of sin, bounded, never accumulated.
tosc(f) = sin(2.0 * library("maths.lib").PI * float(tphase(p, N)) / N)
with {
    toscStep(f) = int(f * 10 + 0.5);          // the integer step, in tenths of a hertz
    p = toscStep(f);
    N = 10 * int(library("maths.lib").SR);    // a tenth of a hertz of resolution
    tphase(p, N) = %(N) ~ +(p);               // the integer phase, exact
};
